window.__vaultPreview("d351f0174d7f3851",{"text":"{\n \"13740\": {\n  \"slug\": \"what-causes-pinhole-leaks-in-copper-pipes\",\n  \"faq\": [\n   [\n    \"Can an epoxy coating stop pinhole leaks in copper pipes?\",\n    \"Yes, when the pipe is still sound enough to coat. The <a href=\\\"https://pipelinersusa.com/epipe-restoration/\\\">ePIPE</a> process dries the pipes with heated air, cleans them with an air and sand mixture, and coats the inside with epoxy, which seals pinholes and protects against new corrosion. The coating is NSF/ANSI 61 certified for drinking water.\"\n   ],\n   [\n    \"How do you find a pinhole leak you cannot see?\",\n    \"A water meter that keeps moving with every tap and appliance off is a common first sign. Pipeliners locates hidden leaks with pressure testing, acoustic listening and thermal imaging before anything is opened. Learn about <a href=\\\"https://pipelinersusa.com/leak-detection-services-in-phoenix-arizona/\\\">leak detection in Phoenix</a>.\"\n   ],\n   [\n    \"Should I repipe or coat my copper pipes after a pinhole leak?\",\n    \"It depends on how far the corrosion has spread. Repeat pinhole leaks across the house point to restoring or replacing the whole system rather than patching one spot. Our guide to <a href=\\\"https://pipelinersusa.com/understanding-pipe-restoration-repiping-vs-pipelining/\\\">repiping vs relining</a> compares the two.\"\n   ],\n   [\n    \"Is one pinhole leak a sign of more to come?\",\n    \"Often, yes. Pinholes form where corrosion has thinned the pipe wall, and the same water runs through the rest of the copper, so other sections are usually wearing too. An inspection shows how far it has spread.\"\n   ]\n  ],\n  \"schema\": false,\n  \"note\": \"OTTO already outputs a 1-question FAQPage here, so no second FAQ schema is added.\"\n },\n \"13684\": {\n  \"slug\": \"cipp-vs-traditional-sewer-line-replacement-pros-and-cons\",\n  \"faq\": [\n   [\n    \"Is CIPP cheaper than traditional sewer line replacement?\",\n    \"Usually. Pipeliners' drain lining typically costs 20 to 30 percent less than digging, demolishing and replacing the line, and it avoids most of the concrete, landscaping and driveway repairs that follow a trench.\"\n   ],\n   [\n    \"How long does a CIPP liner last?\",\n    \"Pipeliners cures its liners with UV LED light, and the finished liner carries a 50-year life expectancy. Read more about <a href=\\\"https://pipelinersusa.com/uv-cured-pipe-lining/\\\">UV-cured liners</a>.\"\n   ],\n   [\n    \"When is traditional replacement the better choice?\",\n    \"When a section has fully collapsed, when the line has a deep sag, or when you need a larger pipe. A liner follows the shape of the old pipe, so it cannot fix those problems.\"\n   ],\n   [\n    \"Can I use my drains during a CIPP job?\",\n    \"Not while the liner cures, which takes from about 90 minutes to 12 hours depending on the job. Most jobs are finished in a few hours to a day or two.\"\n   ]\n  ],\n  \"schema\": true,\n  \"note\": \"Removed the duplicated second copy of the article; replaced unverified per-foot prices and the \\\"no plumbing downtime\\\" line with verified facts.\"\n },\n \"13736\": {\n  \"slug\": \"14-warning-signs-your-sewer-pipes-may-be-leaking\",\n  \"faq\": [\n   [\n    \"Can a sewer line leak be fixed without digging?\",\n    \"Often, yes. If the camera shows the pipe still holds its shape, a cured-in-place liner can seal cracks and leaking joints from the inside. A collapsed section usually has to be dug up and replaced first. See how to <a href=\\\"https://pipelinersusa.com/repair-sewer-line-without-digging/\\\">repair a sewer line without digging</a>.\"\n   ],\n   [\n    \"How do you find where a sewer line is leaking?\",\n    \"A sewer camera inspection shows the inside of the line and exactly where cracks, separated joints and roots are, so only the problem area is worked on.\"\n   ],\n   [\n    \"What causes a sewer line to leak?\",\n    \"The most common causes are tree roots growing into joints, cracked or corroded clay and cast iron pipe, and joints that shift as the soil settles.\"\n   ],\n   [\n    \"Is a leaking sewer line an emergency?\",\n    \"A slow leak is not usually an emergency, but it gets worse over time and can wash out the soil under slabs and walkways. Sewage backing up into the house needs attention right away.\"\n   ]\n  ],\n  \"schema\": true,\n  \"note\": \"Existing closing paragraphs (commercial excavation, fixed cost, comprehensive warranty) left as they were; they need Scott to confirm.\"\n },\n \"14947\": {\n  \"slug\": \"is-trenchless-sewer-repair-more-expensive-than-digging\",\n  \"faq\": [\n   [\n    \"How much does trenchless sewer repair cost?\",\n    \"It depends on the length of the run, the pipe size, how the line is reached, how many branch connections have to be reopened, and the condition of the pipe. See <a href=\\\"https://pipelinersusa.com/how-much-does-trenchless-pipe-lining-cost/\\\">what drives the cost of lining a drain</a> for the full list.\"\n   ],\n   [\n    \"Is trenchless sewer repair worth it?\",\n    \"It usually is when the line still holds its shape and runs under concrete, a driveway, landscaping or mature trees, because those are the costs a trench adds. For a fully collapsed section, digging may be the better fix.\"\n   ],\n   [\n    \"Does a trenchless repair last as long as a new pipe?\",\n    \"Pipeliners' UV-cured liners carry a 50-year life expectancy, which is comparable to new pipe for most homes.\"\n   ]\n  ],\n  \"schema\": true,\n  \"note\": \"\"\n },\n \"13720\": {\n  \"slug\": \"should-i-diy-pipe-repair\",\n  \"faq\": [\n   [\n    \"What pipe repairs can a homeowner do themselves?\",\n    \"Small, reachable jobs such as tightening a loose fitting, replacing a worn washer or clearing a simple sink clog with a plunger. Anything buried, inside a wall or under the slab needs a proper diagnosis first.\"\n   ],\n   [\n    \"Why should I avoid chemical drain cleaners?\",\n    \"Harsh chemicals are hard on old metal pipe and do not remove hard scale, so the clog tends to come back. For blockages, Pipeliners recommends <a href=\\\"https://pipelinersusa.com/hydro-jetting/\\\">hydro jetting</a> instead.\"\n   ],\n   [\n    \"Can I line or coat my own pipes?\",\n    \"No. Lining a drain or coating water lines takes a camera inspection, cleaning equipment, the liner or epoxy system and curing equipment, plus the training to install them correctly.\"\n   ],\n   [\n    \"How do I know if a DIY fix did not work?\",\n    \"Clogs that return, a leak that reappears in the same spot, damp walls or floors, or a water meter that keeps moving with everything off. Any of these means it is time for a camera inspection or leak detection.\"\n   ]\n  ],\n  \"schema\": true,\n  \"note\": \"Removed the empty \\\"Introduction\\\" heading. The body is weak filler and needs a full rewrite later.\"\n },\n \"14832\": {\n  \"slug\": \"reline-vs-replace-best-options-for-drain-and-sewer-pipes\",\n  \"faq\": [\n   [\n    \"Is pipe relining cheaper than replacement?\",\n    \"Usually. Pipeliners' drain lining typically costs 20 to 30 percent less than digging and replacing the pipe, and it avoids most of the restoration work that follows excavation.\"\n   ],\n   [\n    \"How long does a relined pipe last?\",\n    \"Pipeliners cures its liners with UV LED light, and the finished liner carries a 50-year life expectancy.\"\n   ],\n   [\n    \"When can a pipe not be relined?\",\n    \"When a section has collapsed, when the line has a deep sag, or when the pipe needs to be larger. A liner follows the shape of the old pipe, so those cases need replacement.\"\n   ],\n   [\n    \"Can part of a line be relined and part replaced?\",\n    \"Yes, and it is common. A single failed section can be dug up and replaced while the rest of the line is relined from the inside.\"\n   ]\n  ],\n  \"schema\": true,\n  \"note\": \"Removed 2 leftover AI-writer notes printed as bullet points.\"\n }\n}"});
